1.9 Foundational Contribution

The primary contribution of GAIA Sentinel, and thus of this dissertation, is to demonstrate that the pieces of a provably safe global AI governance system are not only imaginable but mathematically coherent. By grounding governance in Lyapunov theory, active inference, POMDP belief tracking, spectral graph analysis, and game-theoretic mechanism design, we provide a constructive proof-of-concept: a blueprint for a future in which advanced intelligence can be allowed to flourish without triggering an uncontrollable cascade. The hard problems—measurability, observability gaps, autoimmune control, strategic capture—are not avoided but confronted head-on with formal tools. The work thus establishes a new interdisciplinary field: computational AI immunology, and offers a concrete target for the global technical and policy communities to converge upon.

In the words of Norbert Wiener, “We have modified our environment so radically that we must modify ourselves in order to exist in this new environment.” GAIA Sentinel is a proposal for that necessary modification—not by suppressing the new intelligence, but by embedding it within a self-correcting, immune-competent planetary framework.

